    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to be confused; I apologize for the goblin metaphor earlier, though I must admit, the idea of a goblin guarding a vault is surprisingly accurate for how strict these agents can be! While a lawyer or bank title company is indeed the professional equivalent, the \"goblin\" part is just the intense, rule-following nature of the process.\n\nHere is the actual step-by-step flow of the money in a Seattle home purchase:\n\n1.  **Funds Deposit:** You wire the earnest money deposit and the full purchase price directly to the escrow company's bank account. This money is now frozen and cannot be touched by either you or the seller.\n2.  **Title Search & Clearance:** The escrow officer (or their title company) runs a title search to ensure the seller actually owns the house and there are no liens or lawsuits attached to it. They also coordinate the final walk-through to make sure the house is in the agreed-upon condition.\n3.  **Closing Disclosure:** Once the title is clear and the house is ready, the escrow officer sends you a Closing Disclosure. This is the final checklist where you sign off on the loan amount, the prorated taxes, and",
